+## Integration and execution-start closure
+
+The current integration includes 59d's exact owner-aware width authority and
+its independent widening matrix, without altering its reviewed native code or
+arithmetic proofs. The 60g source ledger restores all five changed production
+files to the complete merged 59d/59e/59f source before the inherited profile
+checks run. Eleven complete source restorations and thirty-three source
+mutation rejections are required. The twelve exact inherited source profiles
+retain all 3,042 inventory rejection controls. On current 60g source, mutations
+of a checker wrapped by the rollout ledger are rejected at that outer exact
+blob boundary before reaching the historical 59d seam check; the fixture
+expectations distinguish those exact errors and preserve historical profiles.
+
+A plan-local registration boundary must remain first and unique. It closes
+consumer registration before native or caller phases execute, while the one
+physical capture phase must still immediately precede validated emission.
+The first boundary must actually execute, so installing a first-ever observer
+from inside a running phase cannot manufacture an unexecuted seal. Removing,
+duplicating or moving the registration boundary fails closed. Two new tests
+cover nine early/runtime registration combinations and four boundary mutations;
+no rejected callback runs or replaces an existing public artifact. Normal
+caller phase inserters still register both consumer roles in either order
+before execution. No native phase implementation or global lifecycle state is
+modified.
